# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree on every platform.
# The repo had drifted: 156 tracked files carried CRLF, including four .qmd
# sources, _common.R, the lordicon extension, and most of data/. That is
# invisible until something rewrites a file wholesale -- a two-line YAML edit to
# D/11, D/12 and E/13 turned into three whole-file diffs, because the tool that
# made it wrote LF back.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate rather than plain `text=auto`. Without it, a checkout on
# Windows converts to CRLF and the drift comes straight back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git decides text-vs-binary by sniffing for a NUL byte in the first 8k, and .ai
# defeats that test: Illustrator writes PDF (`file` reports "PDF document,
# version 1.6"), the header is plain ASCII, and the compressed streams that do
# contain NULs sit past the sniff window. All six carry CRLF today, so a
# normalizing checkout would rewrite bytes inside those streams.
*.ai binary

# Declared rather than left to detection, so the intent survives a file whose
# first 8k happens to look like text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
